@product-owner-reframe
Feature: Product Owner Agent — Structured Product Thinking Pipeline
  As a technical lead building products with the Software Factory pipeline
  I want the Product Owner agent to encode the repeatable process of ideation, feature definition, scope exploration, and dependency mapping
  So that product thinking sessions produce structured output that feeds /feature-spec without relying on ad-hoc Claude Desktop conversations

  Background:
    Given the specialist-agent harness is configured with role "product-owner"
    And the Player agent has product thinking methodology instructions
    And the Coach agent has coverage, grounding, and scope criteria
    And the detection patterns include UNGROUNDED_FEATURE, MISSING_COVERAGE, SCOPE_CREEP, VAGUE_DESCRIPTION, DEPENDENCY_MISSING

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP A: Key Examples — Core capabilities across input modes
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: 'idea' mode is the most common entry point — Rich arrives with a thought from stepping away and wants to explore it
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Idea mode explores a hypothesis against existing context
    Given a problem statement or hypothesis such as "what if we used event sourcing for the audit trail?"
    And optionally existing product documentation and/or an existing build plan
    And the session is invoked in "idea" mode
    When the Player processes the idea against available context
    Then the output should explore the idea's implications for the product roadmap
    And the output should identify which existing epics or features are affected
    And the output should propose new features if the idea implies them
    And the output should ground the exploration in existing product documentation where available
    And the output should include open_questions for areas the idea doesn't fully resolve

  # Why: Doc-based extraction is the immediate use case — turning existing product docs into a structured feature roadmap
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Extract mode produces grounded features from product documentation
    Given a corpus of product documentation totalling at least 100KB
    And the session is invoked in "extract" mode
    When the Player processes the product documentation
    Then the output should be a ProductRoadmap containing at least one epic
    And each epic should contain at least one feature
    And every feature should reference at least one source document section as grounding
    And the output should include a feature_spec_inputs section with per-feature descriptions

  # Why: Greenfield exploration must produce bounded contexts and a feature map from a problem statement alone
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Greenfield mode produces bounded contexts from a problem statement
    Given a problem statement describing a new product domain
    And no existing product documentation
    And the session is invoked in "greenfield" mode
    When the Player processes the problem statement
    Then the output should identify at least two bounded contexts
    And each bounded context should map to at least one epic
    And features within each epic should be scoped to a single bounded context
    And the output should include open_questions listing areas needing product doc creation

  # Why: Incremental evolution is the most common recurring use — "we've built X, what's next?"
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Evolve mode identifies next features given current build state
    Given a corpus of product documentation
    And an existing build plan listing features already implemented or in progress
    When the session is invoked in "evolve" mode
    Then the output should distinguish between implemented, in-progress, and candidate features
    And candidate features should be marked as "new" relative to the existing build plan
    And the output should not re-propose features already marked as implemented

  # Why: Impact analysis maps new requirements against the existing plan
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Impact mode maps new information against existing feature roadmap
    Given a corpus of product documentation
    And an existing ProductRoadmap from a previous session
    And new information from the product owner
    When the session is invoked in "impact" mode with the new information
    Then the output should identify features affected by the new information
    And the output should identify any new features implied by the new information
    And unchanged features should be preserved from the previous roadmap
    And the output should include a change_summary listing what changed and why

  # Why: Scope negotiation helps prioritise a subset of features for a delivery phase
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Scope mode produces a prioritised phase from a feature list
    Given a ProductRoadmap containing at least 10 features across multiple epics
    And a phase constraint such as "Phase 1 — 6 weeks, 1 developer"
    When the session is invoked in "scope" mode
    Then the output should propose a subset of features for the phase
    And the proposed subset should respect dependency ordering
    And the output should include priority_rationale explaining the selection
    And features not included should be listed as deferred with reasoning

  # Why: Coach coverage checking is the key quality advantage over ad-hoc conversations
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Coach detects missing coverage in doc-based extraction
    Given a corpus of 5 product documents covering 5 distinct domain areas
    And the Player output maps features to only 3 of the 5 domain areas
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should report a MISSING_COVERAGE detection finding
    And the finding should identify the 2 uncovered domain areas by document reference
    And the overall score should be penalised by the MISSING_COVERAGE penalty

  # Why: Feature descriptions must be specific enough to feed /feature-spec directly
  @key-example
  Scenario: Feature descriptions are ready for /feature-spec consumption
    Given the Player has generated a ProductRoadmap
    Then each feature in the feature_spec_inputs section should include a description of at least 2 sentences
    And descriptions should use domain language not implementation language
    And descriptions should include at least one concrete behavioural statement
    And each feature_spec_input should be writable as a standalone --from file for /feature-spec

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP B: Boundary Conditions
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: Single doc is the minimum viable input — must still produce useful output
  @boundary
  Scenario: Extract mode handles a single product document
    Given exactly one product document
    And the session is invoked in "extract" mode
    When the Player processes the documentation
    Then the output should contain at least one epic with at least one feature
    And no MISSING_COVERAGE findings should reference documents outside the input set

  # Why: Large corpus must not cause token overflow or loss of coverage
  @boundary
  Scenario: Extract mode handles a corpus exceeding 300KB
    Given a corpus of product documentation totalling more than 300KB
    And the session is invoked in "extract" mode
    When the Player processes the documentation
    Then the output should reference content from documents across the entire corpus
    And no product document should be silently skipped due to token limits
    And if token limits require chunking, the output should note which documents were processed in which pass

  # Why: First run on a project with no build plan — evolve mode must degrade gracefully
  @boundary
  Scenario: Evolve mode with no existing build plan produces a fresh roadmap
    Given a corpus of product documentation
    And no existing build plan or previous ProductRoadmap
    When the session is invoked in "evolve" mode
    Then the output should behave equivalently to "extract" mode
    And a note should indicate that no prior build state was available

  # Why: Edge case where all features are already built
  @boundary
  Scenario: Evolve mode with all features implemented reports completion
    Given a corpus of product documentation
    And an existing build plan where every extractable feature is marked as implemented
    When the session is invoked in "evolve" mode
    Then the output should confirm that the current build plan covers all documented features
    And the output should include a coverage_score of 1.0 or equivalent
    And no new candidate features should be proposed unless the docs contain areas beyond the build plan

  # Why: Scope mode with a constraint that cannot fit any features
  @boundary
  Scenario: Scope mode with an impossibly tight constraint
    Given a ProductRoadmap containing 10 features each estimated at 2 weeks
    And a phase constraint of "Phase 1 — 1 week, 1 developer"
    When the session is invoked in "scope" mode
    Then the output should not propose an empty phase
    And the output should recommend the single smallest feature that fits
    Or the output should flag that no feature fits the constraint and suggest minimum viable scope

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP C: Negative Cases
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: Extract mode with no product docs is invalid — must fail clearly
  @negative
  Scenario: Extract mode rejects invocation with no product documents
    Given no product documentation is provided
    When the session is invoked in "extract" mode
    Then the session should fail with a clear error
    And the error should indicate that extract mode requires at least one product document

  # Why: Coach must catch features the Player invented that aren't in the docs
  @negative
  Scenario: Coach detects ungrounded features
    Given a product document describing only user authentication and authorisation
    And the Player output includes a feature for "AI-powered recommendation engine"
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should report an UNGROUNDED_FEATURE detection finding
    And the finding should identify the hallucinated feature by name
    And the overall score should be penalised by the UNGROUNDED_FEATURE penalty

  # Why: Features that go beyond the documented scope must be flagged
  @negative
  Scenario: Coach detects scope creep beyond documentation
    Given a product document describing a monitoring dashboard with read-only views
    And the Player output includes a feature for "real-time collaborative editing of dashboard layouts"
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should report a SCOPE_CREEP detection finding
    And the finding should explain how the feature exceeds the documented scope

  # Why: Vague feature descriptions are useless for /feature-spec
  @negative
  Scenario: Coach detects feature descriptions too vague for feature-spec
    Given the Player output includes a feature with description "make the system better"
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should report a VAGUE_DESCRIPTION detection finding
    And the finding should explain that the description lacks concrete behavioural statements
    And the finding should suggest what a specific description would look like

  # Why: Features with missing dependencies create unimplementable roadmaps
  @negative
  Scenario: Coach detects missing dependency in feature ordering
    Given the Player output includes feature B that depends on feature A
    And feature A is not present in the roadmap
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should report a DEPENDENCY_MISSING detection finding
    And the finding should identify both the dependent feature and the missing prerequisite

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP D: Edge Cases
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: Product docs may describe overlapping concerns — features must not duplicate
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Extract mode handles overlapping domain areas across documents
    Given two product documents that both describe transaction monitoring from different angles
    When the Player processes the documentation in "extract" mode
    Then features related to transaction monitoring should be consolidated, not duplicated
    And the grounding should reference both source documents

  # Why: New information may contradict existing docs — agent must surface the conflict
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Impact mode surfaces conflicts between new information and existing docs
    Given a product document stating "alerts are email-only"
    And new information from the product owner stating "alerts must support SMS"
    When the session is invoked in "impact" mode
    Then the output should flag the contradiction between the doc and the new information
    And the conflict should appear in the open_questions section for human resolution

  # Why: A feature may span multiple bounded contexts — must be handled explicitly
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Feature spanning multiple bounded contexts is flagged for decomposition
    Given the Player output includes a feature that references capabilities in two different bounded contexts
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should flag the cross-boundary feature for potential decomposition
    And the finding should suggest splitting into bounded-context-specific features

  # Why: Infrastructure features implied by product docs (auth, monitoring) must be captured
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Extract mode identifies implied infrastructure features
    Given product documentation that mentions "secure access for staff" and "audit trail of all actions"
    When the Player processes the documentation in "extract" mode
    Then the output should include features for authentication/authorisation and audit logging
    And these features should be grounded in the product doc references that imply them

  # Why: Priority rationale must be internally consistent even though it's not scored
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Priority rationale is internally consistent with stated dependencies
    Given the Player output proposes building feature B before feature A
    And feature B is listed as depending on feature A
    When the Coach evaluates the output
    Then the Coach should detect the inconsistency between priority order and dependency chain
    And the finding should appear as a note in the evaluation, not as a scored penalty

  # Why: Existing Graphiti knowledge should inform feature extraction
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Knowledge graph context enriches feature extraction
    Given a corpus of product documentation
    And the Graphiti knowledge graph contains ADRs and patterns from a previous architect-agent session on the same project
    When the session is invoked in "extract" mode with knowledge graph enabled
    Then the output should reference relevant ADRs when proposing features that touch architectural boundaries
    And features should align with architectural patterns already recorded in the knowledge graph

  # Why: The output must be deterministically parseable for pipeline consumption
  @edge-case
  Scenario: ProductRoadmap output is valid against the Pydantic model
    Given any successful PO agent session
    When the output is serialised
    Then the output should parse as a valid ProductRoadmap Pydantic model
    And all required fields should be present and non-empty
    And the feature_spec_inputs section should be extractable as standalone files

  # ==========================================================================
  # GROUP E: Edge Case Expansion — Cross-cutting and integration scenarios
  # ==========================================================================

  # Why: PO agent must work with architect agent's output as input context
  @edge-case
  Scenario: PO agent uses architect conversation starter as context
    Given a corpus of product documentation
    And an architect-agent conversation starter for the same project
    When the session is invoked in "extract" mode with the conversation starter as additional context
    Then features should align with the bounded contexts identified in the conversation starter
    And the output should reference the conversation starter's C4 diagrams when mapping features to system boundaries

  # Why: Evolve mode must handle partial builds — some features done, some in progress
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Evolve mode distinguishes between done, in-progress, and candidate features
    Given a build plan with 3 features marked "implemented", 2 marked "in-progress", and 5 not started
    When the session is invoked in "evolve" mode
    Then implemented features should appear as "implemented" with no action required
    And in-progress features should appear as "in-progress" with current scope preserved
    And candidate features should be evaluated for readiness based on dependency chain

  # Why: The PO agent must not repeat the RequireKit mistake — no elicitation questions
  @edge-case @regression
  Scenario: PO agent does not produce elicitation questions as output
    Given any input mode and any product documentation
    When the Player generates a ProductRoadmap
    Then the output should NOT contain a section asking the product owner questions about requirements
    And open_questions should be limited to genuinely ambiguous items that require human judgment
    And the agent should propose concrete features, not ask what features the user wants

  # Why: Mode should be inferable from input shape when not explicitly specified, with confirmation that learns over time
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Agent infers mode from input and confirms with user
    Given an idea statement and some existing product documentation but no mode flag
    When the session is invoked without an explicit mode
    Then the agent should infer the most likely mode from input shape
    And the agent should present a confirmation: "I think you want idea mode — is that right?"
    And the user's confirmation or correction should be recorded to the knowledge graph
    And explicit --mode flag should override inference and skip confirmation
    And inference rules should include: idea statement alone or with context → idea; product docs only → extract; problem statement only with no docs → greenfield; product docs plus build plan → evolve; product docs plus roadmap plus new info → impact; existing roadmap plus phase constraint → scope

  # Why: Learned mode inference should skip confirmation once confidence is high
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Agent skips mode confirmation when Graphiti confidence is high
    Given a corpus of product documentation and no mode flag
    And the knowledge graph contains 5 or more prior confirmations of "extract" mode for similar input patterns
    When the session is invoked without an explicit mode
    Then the agent should infer "extract" mode and proceed without confirmation
    And a log entry should note that confirmation was skipped due to high learned confidence

  # Why: Feature spec inputs must work as actual --from files
  @edge-case @regression
  Scenario: Feature spec inputs are valid standalone files for /feature-spec --from
    Given the Player has generated a ProductRoadmap with feature_spec_inputs
    When each feature_spec_input is saved as a standalone markdown file
    Then each file should be a valid input for /feature-spec --from
    And each file should contain enough context for /feature-spec to generate Gherkin without additional product doc references
    And each file should NOT contain implementation-specific language
